# Every text file checks out with LF on every OS, so a Windows clone holds the same bytes that CI tests, hashes and
# builds. With core.autocrlf=true a Windows checkout turned LF into CRLF: the audit report loader then kept its
# import lines (5 failing tests) and the reviewed unlock-script hash changed (1 failing test).
* text=auto eol=lf
*.gz binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.png binary
*.pdf binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.xlsx binary
*.zip binary
